      "page_title": "Python Lists: Creation & Indexing",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "1. Definition",
          "ink": "green"
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "text": "A list is a ==mutable==, ==ordered== sequence of objects stored in a dynamic array.",
          "frame": "dashed",
          "ink": "green"
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "2. Mechanism",
          "ink": "purple"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Internally uses a **pointer array**",
            "Elements are references, not copies",
            "Dynamic resizing allows growth"
          ],
          "style": "dot",
          "frame": "dashed",
          "ink": "purple"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "python",
          "lines": [
            "fruits = ['apple', 'banana', 'cherry']",
            "print(fruits[0])  # 'apple'",
            "print(fruits[-1]) # 'cherry'"
          ],
          "note": "Zero-based indexing"
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "3. Example",
