    {
      "page_title": "Slicing Syntax & Mutation Safety",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "1. Slicing Definition",
          "ink": "green"
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "text": "Extract sublists using `list[start:stop:step]`. The `stop` index is always **exclusive**.",
          "frame": "dashed",
          "ink": "green"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "python",
          "lines": [
            "nums = [1, 2, 3, 4, 5]",
            "sub = nums[1:4]  # [2, 3, 4]",
            "step = nums[::2] # [1, 3, 5]"
          ],
          "note": "stop index is NOT included"
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "2. Mechanism: Shallow Copy",
          "ink": "purple"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Slicing creates a **new** list object.",
            "It is a shallow copy, not a view.",
            "Modifying the slice does not affect the original."
          ],
          "style": "dot",
          "frame": "dashed",
          "ink": "purple"
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "3. Append vs Extend",
          "ink": "blue"
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "headers": [
            "Method",
            "Input",
            "Result",
            "Time"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "append",
              "[1, 2]",
              "[[1, 2]]",
              "O(1)"
            ],
            [
              "extend",
              "[1, 2]",
              "[1, 2]",
              "O(k)"
            ]
          ],
          "frame": "dashed"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "python",
          "lines": [
            "a = [1]; a.append([2]) # [1, [2]]",
            "b = [1]; b.extend([2]) # [1, 2]"
          ],
          "note": "append adds object, extend adds items"
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "4. Common Mistakes",
          "ink": "red"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "❌ `extend('abc')` splits into `['a','b','c']`.",
            "❌ `b = a` shares reference; `b.append(1)` changes `a`.",
            "✅ Fix: `a = b.copy()` or `a = b[:]` before mutating."
          ],
          "style": "cross",
          "frame": "dashed",
          "ink": "red"
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "5. Complexity & Tips",
          "ink": "blue"
        },
        {
          "type": "sidebox",
          "title": "Performance Notes",
          "items": [
            "Slicing: O(k) where k is slice length.",
            "Copying: O(n) for full list.",
            "Use list comprehension for transformations."
          ],
          "ink": "blue"
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "style": "tip",
          "title": "Pro Tip",
          "text": "Prefer list comprehensions over manual loops for cleaner, faster code."
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "6. Slicing Examples",
          "ink": "green"
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "headers": [
            "Slice",
            "Result",
            "Note"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "nums[1:4]",
              "[2, 3, 4]",
              "Stop exclusive"
            ],
            [
              "nums[::2]",
              "[1, 3, 5]",
              "Step 2"
            ],
            [
              "nums[::-1]",
              "[5, 4, 3, 2, 1]",
              "Reverse"
            ]
          ],
          "frame": "dashed"
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "7. Mutation Pitfalls",
          "ink": "red"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "❌ `b = a` shares the same list object",
            "❌ `b.append(1)` modifies `a` too",
            "✅ Use `a = b.copy()` for independence"
          ],
          "style": "cross",
          "frame": "dashed",
          "ink": "red"
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "8. Copy Strategies",
          "ink": "purple"
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "headers": [
            "Method",
            "Type",
            "Use Case"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "list.copy()",
              "Shallow",
              "Standard safety"
            ],
            [
              "list[:]",
              "Shallow",
              "Quick slice"
            ],
            [
              "copy.deepcopy()",
              "Deep",
              "Nested structures"
            ]
          ],
          "frame": "dashed"
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "9. Deep Copy Example",
          "ink": "blue"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "python",
          "lines": [
            "import copy",
            "orig = [[1, 2], [3, 4]]",
            "deep = copy.deepcopy(orig)",
            "deep[0][0] = 99 # orig unchanged"
          ],
          "note": "Deep copy isolates nested lists"
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "11. Best Practices",
          "ink": "black"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Use `list.copy()` for shallow copies",
            "Use `deepcopy` for nested lists",
            "Prefer comprehensions over loops"
          ],
          "style": "check",
          "frame": "solid",
          "ink": "black"
        }
